an class=3D"t-a">=E2=89=88</span> 500 GB / year
                   kept ~7 years for finance and audit <span class=3D"t-a">=
=E2=89=88</span> 3.5 TB
Route cache        ~1,500 nonstop routes <span class=3D"t-a">=C3=97</span> =
331 days <span class=3D"t-a">=C3=97</span> ~2 KB (that day's flight list) <=
span class=3D"t-a">=E2=89=88</span> 1 GB <span class=3D"t-a">=E2=86=92</spa=
n> Redis</code></pre></div><h4>Key insights</h4><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span =
class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Search is the volume pro=
blem:</strong> 1,000 reads per write. Cache it, and never let search touch =
the inventory database directly.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</spa=
n><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Booking is the correctness problem:</stron=
g> only ~120 writes a second at a fare-sale peak, but many land on the same=
 flight at the same time.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div =
class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>One booking =3D one flight, and the data is small=
:</strong> ~27 GB of seats and ~500 GB of bookings a year fit on one Postgr=
eSQL primary, so <strong>no sharding</strong>. Every hold, payment commit a=
nd cancellation is a single database transaction.</p></div></li></ol></deta=
ils></section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"-api-design"><span class=3D"=
sec-n">5.</span> API Design</h2><p class=3D"lead">APIs called by the web an=
d mobile apps (partners use the same APIs through a partner gateway). All f=
ields use camelCase. Money is in minor units (cents) to avoid floating-poin=
t errors.</p><h3 id=3D"1-search-flights">1. Search Flights</h3><div class=
=3D"endpoint"><span class=3D"m m-get">GET</span><code>/v1/flights/search</c=
ode></div><p>Find nonstop flights and fares on one route for one day. Resul=
ts come from cache, so they can be a few seconds stale.</p><h4>Headers</h4>=
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">HTTP headers</span></div><pre><code>=
<span class=3D"t-c">// 1. X-Request-Id =E2=80=94 traces this one request ac=
ross gateway =E2=86=92 services =E2=86=92 caches</span>
<span class=3D"t-h">X-Request-Id</span>: req_3f9a21c7</code></pre></div><h4=
>Query parameters</h4><div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span cla=
ss=3D"dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">JSON</span></d=
iv><pre><code>{
