s=3D"t-s">"12C"</span> }
}</code></pre></div><h4>Notes</h4><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1<=
/span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>All or nothing:</strong> every passeng=
er and every chosen seat is held, or nothing is. It's one database transact=
ion.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p>201=
, not 202: the hold finishes during the request (~100=E2=80=93300 ms), and =
the user needs the answer now.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span>=
<div class=3D"li-b"><p>Errors: 409 <code>SEAT_UNAVAILABLE</code> (lists the=
 seats) =C2=B7 409 <code>FARE_SOLD_OUT</code> =C2=B7 409 <code>PRICE_CHANGE=
D</code> (with the new price; the user must accept it) =C2=B7 429 too many =
active holds for this user.</p></div></li></ol><h3 id=3D"why-two-calls-hold=
-first-then-pay">Why two calls: hold first, then pay?</h3><div class=3D"cal=
lout tip"><div class=3D"ct">One-line answer</div><p>the user must know thei=
r seats are secured <strong>before</strong> they pay, and payment can take =
minutes (card entry, 3-D Secure), so we lock first and charge second, exact=
ly like a movie booking.</p></div><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1<=
/span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Without a hold:</strong> the user type=
s card details for 3 minutes, pays, and then learns 12A was sold to someone=
 else. We'd have to refund.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><di=
v class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>With a hold:</strong> the seats are theirs for =
15 minutes, shown with a countdown; payment just confirms them.</p></div></=
li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cost:</stro=
ng> abandoned holds block seats for up to 15 minutes, so holds must expire =
automatically (Deep Dive 2) and be limited per user (Deep Dive 8).</p></div=
></li></ol><h3 id=3D"4-pay--confirm">4. Pay &amp; Confirm</h3><div class=3D=
"endpoint"><span class=3D"m m-post">POST</span><code>/v1/bookings/{pnr}/pay=
ments</code></div><p>Pay for a <code>HELD</code> booking. On success, the s=
eats become <code>BOOKED</code> and e-tickets are issued.</p><h4>Headers</h=
4><div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><=
i></i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">HTTP headers</span></div><pre><cod=
e><span class=3D"t-c">// 1. Authorization =E2=80=94 the same user (or guest=
 session) that created the hold</span>
<span class=3D"t-h">Authorization</span>: Bearer &lt;user-token&gt;

<span class=3D"t-c">// 2. Content-Type =E2=80=94 the body is JSON</span>
<span class=3D"t-h">Content-Type</span>: application/json</code></pre></div=
><h4>Request</h4><div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D=
"dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">JSON</span></div><p=
re><code>{
  <span class=3D"t-c">// 1. idempotencyKey =E2=80=94 one per "Pay" click. A=
lso sent to the payment gateway,</span>
  <span class=3D"t-c">//    so a double click or retry can never charge twi=
ce</span>
