fka.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">8</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><st=
rong>Return 200</strong> with the tickets.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D=
"n">9</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Async from Kafka:</strong> Notif=
ication Service sends the confirmation and e-tickets; Secure Flight receive=
s passenger data; Search Indexer updates seat counts.</p></div></li></ol><p=
><strong>Why authorize =E2=86=92 commit =E2=86=92 capture</strong> (AlgoMas=
ter, Shopify 6.4): if the commit fails for any reason, we <strong>void</str=
ong> the authorization, which is instant and free. Capturing first would fo=
rce a refund, which takes days and may cost fees.</p><h4>If something crash=
es (the payment reconciler)</h4><p>A reconciler runs every minute and finds=
 bookings stuck in <code>PAYMENT_PENDING</code> or <code>CONFIRMED</code> f=
or more than 2 minutes (<code>INDEX (status, updated_at)</code>). Each step=
 stored its result, so it resumes from where the crash happened:</p><ol cla=
ss=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cras=
h before authorize:</strong> the gateway has no payment for that key. Relea=
se the holds to <code>ACTIVE</code> (or let them expire), booking back to <=
code>HELD</code> / <code>EXPIRED</code>. Nothing charged.</p></div></li><li=
><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Crash after autho=
rize, before commit:</strong> ask the gateway by idempotency key =E2=86=92 =
<code>AUTHORIZED</code>. The holds are still <code>CONFIRMING</code>, so co=
mmit, capture and ticket. The user gets their booking.</p></div></li><li><s=
pan class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Crash after commit, =
before capture:</strong> seats are <code>BOOKED</code>, payment <code>AUTHO=
RIZED</code> =E2=86=92 capture, then ticket.</p></div></li><li><span class=
=3D"n">4</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Crash after capture, before t=
icketing:</strong> booking <code>CONFIRMED</code> =E2=86=92 issue tickets.<=
/p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">5</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>=
Gateway timeout (we don't know if it authorized):</strong> never assume fai=
lure. Query the gateway (AlgoMaster's <code>handle_timeout</code>); <code>U=
NKNOWN</code> after several tries =E2=86=92 void if possible and alert supp=
ort.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">6</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><st=
rong><code>CONFIRMING</code> hold older than its expiry:</strong> only the =
reconciler may release it, and only after it has voided (or confirmed no) a=
uthorization. So seats are never released while money is held.</p></div></l=
i><li><span class=3D"n">7</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Why it's saf=
e:</strong> every step is idempotent (hold ID, payment idempotency key, <co=
de>WHERE hold_id =3D ours</code>), so repeating a step changes nothing; the=
 reconciler only moves bookings forward or voids.</p></div></li></ol><div c=
lass=3D"callout interview"><div class=3D"ct">=F0=9F=92=AC Interview line</d=
iv><p>"Payment first freezes the holds so they can't expire mid-payment, th=
en authorizes the card, commits the seats, captures, and issues tickets. Ev=
ery step is idempotent and its result is stored, so a reconciler can finish=
 or roll back any booking that crashed halfway: capture if seats were commi=
tted, void if they weren't."</p></div><h3 id=3D"5-flow-hold-expiry">5. Flow=
