n class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> one sta=
tement, one round trip. The row lock lasts microseconds. The condition <str=
ong>is</strong> the check, so there's nothing to retry: of two requests for=
 12A, exactly one changes 1 row.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span clas=
s=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> the caller on=
ly learns "not all seats were free", so it re-reads to say which (cheap).</=
p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>D=
eadlocks:</strong> two overlapping multi-seat holds could in theory lock ro=
ws in different orders. We sort the seat numbers before the update and the =
index is scanned in key order, so both lock in the same order. If a deadloc=
k ever happens, PostgreSQL aborts one transaction; we return 409 and the us=
er picks again.</p></div></li></ol><h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap=
-tag">Approach 4</span>Redis distributed lock <span class=3Dap-src>(AlgoMas=
ter movie, Approach 2)</span></h4><div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-ba=
r"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">Lu=
a</span></div><pre><code><span class=3D"t-c">-- KEYS =3D lock:flight:DL2301=
-20261220:seat:12A, =E2=80=A6:12C   ARGV =3D holdId, ttlSeconds</span>
<span class=3D"t-k">local</span> acquired =3D {}
<span class=3D"t-k">for</span> i, key <span class=3D"t-k">in</span> <span c=
lass=3D"t-k">ipairs</span>(KEYS) <span class=3D"t-k">do</span>
  <span class=3D"t-k">if</span> redis.call(<span class=3D"t-s">'SET'</span>=
, key, ARGV[<span class=3D"t-n">1</span>], <span class=3D"t-s">'NX'</span>,=
 <span class=3D"t-s">'EX'</span>, ARGV[<span class=3D"t-n">2</span>]) <span=
 class=3D"t-k">then</span>
    table.insert(acquired, key)
  <span class=3D"t-k">else</span>
    <span class=3D"t-k">for</span> _, k <span class=3D"t-k">in</span> <span=
 class=3D"t-k">ipairs</span>(acquired) <span class=3D"t-k">do</span> redis.=
call(<span class=3D"t-s">'DEL'</span>, k) <span class=3D"t-k">end</span>   =
<span class=3D"t-c">-- all or nothing</span>
    <span class=3D"t-k">return</span> <span class=3D"t-k">nil</span>
  <span class=3D"t-k">end</span>
<span class=3D"t-k">end</span>
<span class=3D"t-k">return</span> acquired</code></pre></div><ol class=3D"n=
l"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><stro=
ng>Pros:</strong> under 1 ms; the Lua script makes a multi-seat lock all-or=
-nothing; the TTL releases abandoned seats by itself.</p></div></li><li cla=
ss=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</=
strong> a second system next to the database; Redis replicates asynchronous=
ly, so a failover can lose a lock (split-brain) and let a second user lock =
12A; Redis and the database can drift apart.</p></div></li></ol><h4 class=
=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 5</span>Two-phase reservation=
 <span class=3Dap-src>(AlgoMaster movie, Approach 3, <strong>their recommen=
dation</strong>)</span></h4><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span>=
<div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Phase 1, soft lock (Redis):</strong> at "Res=
erve", run the Lua lock above with a 10-minute TTL; also save the reservati=
on in the database as <code>pending</code>, so ownership survives a Redis o=
utage.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><=
strong>Phase 2, hard lock (database):</strong> at payment, check the Redis =
locks are still held, charge with an idempotency key, mark seats <code>book=
ed</code> in a transaction, then delete the locks.</p></div></li><li><span =
class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>If the database update f=
ails after payment:</strong> refund (saga).</p></div></li></ol><p><strong>W=
hy we don't follow AlgoMaster's recommendation for airlines</strong> <span =
class=3D"pill our">our addition</span>:</p><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=
=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Load:</strong> a blockbuster =
opening sends 100=E2=80=931000=C3=97 traffic at one show. Our peak is ~360 =
holds/s across <strong>all</strong> flights, and each is one ~1 ms statemen=
t. The database alone is fast enough, so Redis buys nothing.</p></div></li>=
<li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>One source of =
truth:</strong> with two-phase, "is 12A held?" has two answers (Redis and t=
he database) that must be kept in sync.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n"=
>3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>AlgoMaster's own edge case:</strong=
> the Redis lock can expire while the bank is processing, someone else take=
s the seats, and the user must be refunded. We freeze the hold in the datab=
ase before charging (Deep Dive 2), so that path can't happen.</p></div></li=
><li><span class=3D"n">4</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>When we'd swi=
tch:</strong> if a single flight ever saw thousands of holds per second, pu=
t the Redis lock in front as a fast filter and keep the database update as =
the final check.</p></div></li></ol><h4>Comparison</h4><div class=3D"tbl"><=
table><thead><tr><th style=3D"text-align:left">Approach</th><th style=3D"te=
xt-align:left">Correctness</th><th style=3D"text-align:left">Throughput</th=
><th style=3D"text-align:left">Complexity</th><th style=3D"text-align:left"=
>Fit for us</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left">Pessi=
mistic <code>FOR UPDATE</code></td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Strong</td=
><td style=3D"text-align:left">Low under contention</td><td style=3D"text-a=
lign:left">Low (watch lock order)</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">OK, but=
 slower</td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left">Optimistic version</td><=
td style=3D"text-align:left">Strong</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Mediu=
m (retries)</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Medium</td><td style=3D"text-=
align:left">OK</td></tr><tr class=3D"hl"><td style=3D"text-align:left"><str=
ong>Atomic conditional update</strong></td><td style=3D"text-align:left"><s=
trong>Strong</strong></td><td style=3D"text-align:left"><strong>High (one s=
tatement)</strong></td><td style=3D"text-align:left"><strong>Low</strong></=
td><td style=3D"text-align:left"><strong><span class=3D"ok">=E2=9C=93</span=
> our choice</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left">Redis lock=
 (<code>SET NX EX</code> + Lua)</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Hint only=
