<td style=3D"text-align:left">Medium</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Only=
 as a pre-filter for extreme spikes</td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:le=
ft">Two-phase (Redis + DB), AlgoMaster's pick</td><td style=3D"text-align:l=
eft">Strong (DB is final)</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">High</td><td st=
yle=3D"text-align:left">Higher (two systems in sync)</td><td style=3D"text-=
align:left">Movie blockbusters; not needed at our load</td></tr></tbody></t=
able></div><p><strong>Why the database is enough here:</strong> even at a f=
are-sale peak we do ~360 holds per second across all flights, and each touc=
hes only ~2=E2=80=934 rows. PostgreSQL does thousands of these per second. =
Redis would add a second system to keep in sync for throughput we don't nee=
d. <span class=3D"pill our">our addition</span></p><div class=3D"callout in=
terview"><div class=3D"ct">=F0=9F=92=AC Interview line</div><p>"Every seat =
is a row, and the hold is one conditional update: AVAILABLE or expired HELD=
 =E2=86=92 HELD with our hold ID. The database guarantees only one request =
can match, so there's no lock to manage and no double-assigned seat. I'd ad=
d a Redis pre-filter only if a single flight saw thousands of holds per sec=
ond, which airlines don't."</p></div><h3 id=3D"deep-dive-2-how-do-you-hold-=
seats-while-the-user-pays-and-release-them-if-they-dont" class=3D"dd"><span=
 class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 2</span><span class=3D"dd-q">How do you hold seat=
s while the user pays, and release them if they don't?</span></h3><p>This i=
s AlgoMaster's <strong>reservation with TTL</strong> (Shopify 6.2, Approach=
 3): <code>available =E2=86=92 held =E2=86=92 sold</code>, and held goes ba=
ck to available on expiry.</p><h4>Ways to expire a hold</h4><div class=3D"t=
bl"><table><thead><tr><th style=3D"text-align:left">Option</th><th style=3D=
"text-align:left">How</th><th style=3D"text-align:left">Problem</th></tr></=
thead><tbody><tr class=3D"hl"><td style=3D"text-align:left"><strong>DB <cod=
e>expires_at</code> + sweeper (our choice)</strong></td><td style=3D"text-a=
lign:left">Sweeper releases <code>ACTIVE</code> holds past <code>expires_at=
</code> every 30 s</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Up to 30 s late =E2=86=
=92 fixed by lazy expiry</td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left"><strong=
>Lazy expiry (our addition)</strong></td><td style=3D"text-align:left">The =
hold query treats <code>HELD</code> with <code>hold_expires_at &lt; now()</=
code> as free</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Counters still need the swe=
eper</td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left">Redis key TTL + keyspace no=
tifications</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Key expires, a listener relea=
ses the seat</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Notifications are fire-and-f=
orget: a disconnected listener misses them, and the seat stays held forever=
</td></tr><tr><td style=3D"text-align:left">Delay queue (e.g. SQS delay)</t=
d><td style=3D"text-align:left">Send "check hold h1" with a 15-minute delay=
</td><td style=3D"text-align:left">Extra system; a hold extended during pay=
ment needs the message re-sent (SQS max delay is 15 min)</td></tr></tbody><=
/table></div><p><strong>Same idea as AlgoMaster's "Hybrid (Recommended)" ex=
piry:</strong> they combine a Redis TTL (seats free at 10 minutes), an acti=
ve check when serving seat maps (show expired holds as available), and a cl=
eanup job every minute (fix the database). We get the same three layers on =
one database row: <code>hold_expires_at</code> (the TTL), the lazy check in=
side the hold query, and the 30-second sweeper.</p><h4>The race everyone fo=
rgets: payment vs expiry</h4><ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span=
><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Problem:</strong> the user clicks Pay at 14=
:58. The bank takes 5 seconds. At 15:00 the sweeper releases the seats and =
someone else holds them. At 15:03 the payment succeeds: the user is charged=
 for seats they don't have.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><di=
v class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Fix:</strong> step 3 of Flow 4 moves the hold t=
o <code>CONFIRMING</code> and extends it <strong>before</strong> calling th=
e bank, with a condition (<code>status =3D &#x27;ACTIVE&#x27; AND expires_a=
t &gt; now()</code>). Either we freeze it first (and the sweeper ignores it=
), or the sweeper released it first (and we return 410 without charging). N=
ever both.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b">=
<p><strong>Commit is guarded too:</strong> <code>UPDATE =E2=80=A6 WHERE hol=
